    "summary": "Observe independent missing-codec REDs, install deterministic math-ir/1 JSON serialization and decoding of exact rationals, binary64 bits, units, symbols, matrices, operations and restrictions, and verify ten round-trip oracles and full regressions.",
    "value": "Preserves exact quantities and scope/domain semantics across a reusable .NET JSON transport without implicit numeric widening or provider-specific AST dependencies.",
    "debtChanges": [
      "T2 remains open for adversarial JSON decoding, duplicate and unknown keys, scope integrity and distinct semantic/presentation hashes.",
      "Canonical structural byte identity is not an algebraic equivalence proof; OpenMath/MathML adapters remain future work.",
      "No external AURA adoption or publication is claimed."
    ],
    "nextAction": "Qualify M2-W01-C03-T2 with independent adversarial JSON decoder and hash tests before completing the codec chunk.",
    "achievements": [
